On 2020-03-23 08:32, Anshuman Gupta wrote:=0A=
> Some times delayed audio codec disabling causes failure=0A=
> of test, using igt_wait to check lpsp after disabling all outputs.=0A=
=0A=
Seems like this answers my question on patch 2/5: We are sending audio=0A=
to the screen even when we do not have anything to send...=0A=
=0A=
I know there are some screens that take ages to re-enable sound after=0A=
not getting any for a while, but waiting 10 or even 30s without sound=0A=
before disabling it does not sound like a terrible idea. My TV=0A=
automatically disables sound after way less than that anyway.=0A=
=0A=
So, to me, this is a driver bug.=0A=
=0A=
That being said, the patch is fine even if your reason for it is not=0A=
acceptable.=0A=
=0A=
Martin=0A=
